---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Fabriant | Weaving Intelligence into Cloud
ogTitle: Fabriant | Leave your Azure to us. Focus on growing your business.
description: Fabriant runs and improves the Azure platform under your product (releases, security, cost and compliance) so your team can focus on growing the business. Certified engineers, fixed-scope sprints, and a free 1-week cloud assessment to start.
ogDescription: Senior Azure expertise, on demand. Microsoft-certified engineers, fixed-scope sprints and a complimentary 1-week assessment to start.
---
      <!-- Hero: what we do, in one line -->
      <section class="hero hero-solo">
        <div>
          <div class="badge">Azure platform engineering · Microsoft AI Cloud Partner</div>
          <h1>Leave your Azure cloud to us. <span class="hero-accent">Focus on growing your business.</span></h1>
          <p class="hero-lead">
            Fabriant takes care of the Azure platform under your product: safe releases, strong security, a lower bill and audit-ready controls. Your team stays on the features your customers pay for.
          </p>
          <p class="hero-pitch"><strong>Senior Azure expertise, on demand.</strong> Microsoft-certified engineers who work as an extension of your team, with an agreed scope and clear outcomes. Start with a complimentary one-week assessment.</p>
          <div class="hero-actions">
            <a class="cta" href="/contact/?topic=free-assessment">Get your free 1-week assessment</a>
            <a class="cta-secondary" href="#services-preview">See what we do</a>
          </div>
          <ul class="proof-strip">
            <li>Member of the Microsoft AI Cloud Partner Program</li>
            <li>Microsoft-certified engineers (AZ-305, AZ-104)</li>
            <li>Fixed-scope sprints</li>
            <li>One team across time zones</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Why: the problems we take off your plate -->
      <section id="overview">
        <div class="section-header">
          <h2>Azure problems are business problems</h2>
          <p>A failed release costs revenue. An unexplained bill costs margin. A weak control costs you the audit. We take care of the Azure platform underneath your product so those stop happening.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cards cards-4">
          <div class="card">
            <h3>Releases that break production</h3>
            <p class="card-text">Health-gated rollouts that catch a bad release early and roll it back before customers feel it.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="card">
            <h3>An Azure bill that keeps rising</h3>
            <p class="card-text">Clear cost visibility, rightsizing and tagging, with savings reported as estimated, implemented and realized.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="card">
            <h3>Audit and security pressure</h3>
            <p class="card-text">Policy, identity and AKS controls mapped to the evidence your auditors ask for.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="card">
            <h3>A platform team at capacity</h3>
            <p class="card-text">Certified engineers who join your team and work to your backlog.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- What: services in detail -->
      <section id="services-preview">
        <div class="section-header">
          <h2>What we do</h2>
          <p>Five ways we help, each tied to a problem your business already feels.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cards offering-cards">
          {%- for offering in offerings %}
          <div class="card offering">
            <h3><a href="/services/#{{ offering.id }}">{{ offering.name }}</a></h3>
            <p class="offering-value">{{ offering.value }}</p>
            <ul class="list">
              {%- for point in offering.points %}
              <li><span class="dot"></span>{{ point }}</li>
              {%- endfor %}
            </ul>
          </div>
          {%- endfor %}
        </div>
        <div class="section-actions">
          <a class="cta-secondary" href="/services/">See all services</a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Who, where, when: why Fabriant -->
      <section id="why-fabriant">
        <div class="section-header">
          <h2>Why teams choose Fabriant</h2>
          <p>Senior Azure engineering when you need it, without the cost and delay of building a platform team.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cards cards-4">
          <div class="card">
            <h3>Fixed scope, fixed outcome</h3>
            <p class="card-text">Every sprint has an agreed scope, a set duration and evidence that it worked. No open-ended billing.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="card">
            <h3>Yours to keep</h3>
            <p class="card-text">Everything is built as code in your repositories and your Azure tenant, with runbooks and a handover to your team.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="card">
            <h3>Certified and recognized</h3>
            <p class="card-text">Microsoft-certified engineers and a member of the Microsoft AI Cloud Partner Program.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="card">
            <h3>Work moves while you sleep</h3>
            <p class="card-text">A U.S. registered company with engineers in Pune, India, so work continues across time zones with daily overlap.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="segments">
          <div class="segment">
            <h3>Growing software companies</h3>
            <p>B2B SaaS, commerce, fintech and healthtech teams running production on Azure, often on AKS, with a small or no platform team.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="segment">
            <h3>Larger Azure estates</h3>
            <p>Organisations with many subscriptions and a landing zone whose in-house platform team needs more hands.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- How: getting started -->
      <section id="get-started">
        <div class="section-header">
          <h2>How to start</h2>
          <p>Most clients begin with a free one-week assessment. You can be up and running within days.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="start-layout">
          <div class="grid process">
            <div class="step">
              <h4>Talk to us</h4>
              <p>A 30-minute call about your Azure setup and what is getting in the way.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="step">
              <h4>Free assessment</h4>
              <p>One week, read-only access. We find the reliability, security and cost hotspots.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="step">
              <h4>Fix and hand over</h4>
              <p>A fixed-scope sprint or ongoing engineers, ending with work your team owns.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="hero-card">
            <div class="hero-card-label">Start here · Complimentary</div>
            <h3>Cloud Assessment Sprint</h3>
            <p class="hero-card-sub">One week. Read-only access. No fee, no obligation.</p>
            <ul class="list">
              <li><span class="dot"></span>One subscription or priority workload</li>
              <li><span class="dot"></span>Reliability, security and cost hotspots</li>
              <li><span class="dot"></span>Executive readout and quick wins</li>
              <li><span class="dot"></span>A recommended next step</li>
            </ul>
            <a class="cta start-cta" href="/contact/?topic=free-assessment">Request your free assessment</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="section-actions">
          <a class="cta-secondary" href="/how-to-start/">See all ways to engage</a>
        </div>
      </section>

      {%- if collections.posts and collections.posts.length %}
      <!-- Latest articles (shown once at least one post is published) -->
      <section id="latest-articles">
        <div class="section-header">
          <h2>Latest articles</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="post-list">
          {%- for post in collections.posts | head(3) %}
          <a class="card card-link post-card" href="{{ post.url }}">
            <p class="post-meta"><time datetime="{{ post.date | isoDate }}">{{ post.date | readableDate }}</time></p>
            <h3>{{ post.data.title }}</h3>
            <p class="card-text">{{ post.data.description }}</p>
          </a>
          {%- endfor %}
        </div>
        <div class="section-actions">
          <a class="cta-secondary" href="/engineering/">All articles</a>
        </div>
      </section>
      {%- endif %}
